{"slug":"chainquery","fork":"Blockchains/chainquery","upstream":"OdyseeTeam/chainquery","branch":"master","commit":"f18fada24853fca3c5bad907937d9fdacf3d3aae","indexed_at":"2026-10-04T16:40:01Z","category":"chains-protocols","description":"Chainquery parses and syncs the LBRY blockchain data into structured SQL","readme_summary":"Chainquery reads the LBRY blockchain into a structured **MySQL** database so that blocks, transactions, addresses, and the full LBRY **claim** system (channels, publishes, supports, tips/purchases, tags) can be queried quickly with plain SQL instead of walking the chain over RPC. It connects to a LBRY full node over JSON-RPC \u2014 **lbcd** in production (LBRY's Go full-node implementation, which the stack has migrated to), or the original **lbrycrd** \u2014 ingests blocks as they are mined, keeps the database in sync (including across blockchain reorganizations), computes derived data via scheduled jobs, and exposes an HTTP API \u2014 including a public, read-only SQL endpoint. Everything runs from a single binary (`chainquery serve`), which starts the API server and the daemon together. There are four logical parts.","install_commands":["git clone https://github.com/lbryio/chainquery.git","go build -o chainquery .","go test -race ./..."],"languages_bytes":{"Go":1247592,"JavaScript":154369,"Python":79161},"file_count":257,"total_bytes":1939348,"licenses":[{"path":"LICENSE","detected":"MIT","head":"MIT License Copyright (c) 2018-2020 LBRY Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal in t"}],"license_spdx_github":"MIT","spdx_headers":{},"packages":[{"ecosystem":"go","name":"github.com/lbryio/chainquery","path":"go.mod","dependencies":["github.com/DATA-DOG/go-sqlmock","github.com/OdyseeTeam/sockety","github.com/btcsuite/btcd","github.com/btcsuite/btcutil","github.com/fatih/color","github.com/friendsofgo/errors","github.com/fsnotify/f